From a40c158fe49a4d04e252f8078adaaec7883e7c5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:42:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(setup): align the part to a setup's own frame,
 separate from the work offset

A setup can hold the part flipped or turned: SetupDef.part_alignment, a
rigid transform document -> setup frame (None = as modelled), set by the
undoable AlignPartToSetup (any rigid transform, presets, or typed X/Y/Z
angles about the parts' centre). Only parts read through it; the setup's
stock, offsets and fixtures already live in the setup frame. The work
offset (setup::wcs_slot) is untouched; rotated offsets stay refused.

- The following stock is rebuilt square to the setup frame; a cylinder
  that would lie down or a shared stock is refused by name. MoveModel
  conjugates the move for an aligned setup's stock; a datum transfer
  carries the alignment.
- Generation (material, model/selection heights), stamps, the program
  sim's part, stock fit, stock from model and the viewport's drawing and
  picks read in the setup frame. As modelled every read is the old call,
  so paths, stamps and posts are byte-identical.
- In an aligned setup only Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive on
  a whole model or the stock generate; other kinds, picks, area controls,
  tilts and non-mill machines are refused by name at collect_job. The
  program sim refuses a program spanning differently-held setups.
- Project v53: setup.part_alignment; absent = as modelled (v52 files load
  unchanged); a non-rigid transform is corrupt.
- Setups page: Part alignment combo plus typed angles (AlignPart).

Fixes #326

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
